{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789908076,"nonce":"V2qBSdd//tqGC0AjNhiJjWHz2Nk=","message":"Landed in e2314a6e (with 483e53bb for the Cranelift parameter mapping it\nexposed).\n\nWhat changed: an interpreted frame that warms leaves into a function\noutlined from the region its header reaches (osr::outline), optimised in\nthe bead's scratch module and compiled by Cranelift, entered through an\nadapter published at the frame's site. The interpreter runs the module's\nbody as lowered plus the release pass alone (2 ms over float's 29\nloop-bearing bodies against 24 ms for the whole pipeline), so a function\nthat runs once is never optimised, and the region inherits the releases\ninside it. The LLVM tier compiles the region too and publishes its resume\npoints under the bead at the region's sites, so a single long call moves\nto LLVM mid-loop (test: a_frame_in_the_outlined_region_moves_to_the_\noptimizing_tier). Whichever promotion runs first, the interpreted\nrequest's or the region's own probes', takes the pending regions\n(outlined_regions); the race was real and lost the LLVM region one run\nin two before that. Cells publish at the outline's install: the adapter\nreaches the region through its cell. ZYNTAX_DISABLE_OUTLINE=1 bisects\nback to the baseline resume point.\n\nQuiet NUC, tiered with LLVM, ZYPY_LLVM=1, 50 iterations, two runs each,\nbase = 185882e:\n\n  kernel     wall base -\u003e new     it1 base -\u003e new   steady (last10)\n  float      257/370 -\u003e 274/280   35.0 -\u003e 38.7/41.4 3.0/3.2 -\u003e 3.2/3.3\n  nbody      366/374 -\u003e 355/369   31.8/38.6 -\u003e 41    4.5/4.8 -\u003e 4.5/4.7\n  richards   173/191 -\u003e 170/171   1.3/1.4 -\u003e 1.2/1.8 0.90 -\u003e 0.92/0.96\n  fannkuch   1657/1673 -\u003e 1591/1640  46.5/46.9 -\u003e 60.9/64.8  31.4/31.9 -\u003e 30.2/30.7\n  meteor     2331/2373 -\u003e 2335/2355  99/101 -\u003e 105/106  40.8/41.8 -\u003e 40.3/41.5\n\nThe walls hold or improve; the first iteration is slower because the\nregion's optimisation (fannkuch: 8.7 ms pipeline + 3.7 ms Cranelift)\nnow falls inside it, where the up-front optimisation of every body fell\nbefore it (the ask comes 21 ms earlier). Followed in 9f95f2b. float's\nsteady state depends on what the collector retains, 93c247d.","files":null}]}